  "category": "navigation",
  "description": "Atlas sidebar navigation item: a 70x52 vertical stack (icon over label) with three interaction states (default, hover, selected). Unlike the ShowUp `nav-item` component (which has multiple unresolved literal bindings — see token-gaps.md), this component is fully and correctly tokenized in Figma: every styled property on every layer resolves to a named Figma variable with a matching `--klp-*` alias. No token gaps on the component's own layers (root/icon/label); the single gap recorded below is on an internal geometry property of the nested icon-selector sub-instance, not on navbar-item itself.",
  "radixPrimitive": "@radix-ui/react-slot",
  "anatomy": [
    {
      "part": "root",
      "element": "button",
      "notes": "70x52 vertical flex stack (flex-col items-center justify-center), paddingY 4px each side, gap 4px between icon and label. No horizontal padding. asChild-friendly so consumers can render as <a> for real navigation links."
    },
    {
      "part": "icon",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "70x24 lucide-react icon slot (NOT a klp component reuse per explicit instruction — the Figma 'Icon selector' instance is treated purely as an icon-rendering slot). Sample glyph resolves to lucide 'search'. Centered, 2px inset padding (--klp-size-4xs) on all sides around a 20x20 icon box; the icon glyph itself renders at 15x15 with a 1.5px stroke weight (literal, not bound to a variable)."
    },
    {
      "part": "label",
      "element": "span",
      "notes": "70x16 TEXT node, sample copy \"Search\", centered, single line, fully token-bound (fill, fontSize, fontWeight, fontFamily)."
    }
